{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:30:29.047Z","data":{"text":"Done. All acceptance lines are covered and both verifies pass.\n\n**Summary of the work:**\n\n- **`src/watcher/plan-conflict.ts`** (new): `findPlanConflict` decides whether the last red change-verify run is a plan conflict — run not timed out, `readFailingTestFiles` names at least one test, and every named test is outside the current task's resolved scope and owned by another task of the same change with a `.run/done/` marker. Ownership comes from each done task's resolved `tasks/<n>.md` scope and its `Touched:` line (via `parseResultSections`), with the lowest task number named. `formatPlanConflictMarker` builds the `blocked` dead marker with the failing-tests lines, `osq plan <id>`, and the excerpt as `formatChangeVerifyMarker` builds it.\n- **`src/watcher/change-verify.ts`**: `runChangeVerifyGate` calls `findPlanConflict` after the rerun loop when the rerun context is given and the result is red, returning a failure with `reason: 'blocked'`, the marker, and the `Plan conflict: ...` error; all failures now carry an explicit reason (`change_verify_red` otherwise). Tagged with `@scenario`/`@adr 006`.\n- **`src/watcher/runner.ts`**: one-line change — `fail(gate.reason, gate.marker, gate.error, gate.extra)`; line count and `runTask` length unchanged.\n- **`tests/change-verify-plan-conflict.test.ts`** (new): 9 plain `node:test` cases proving every row of the \"Failing tests owned by an earlier task\" table through `runTask`, the full \"Plan conflict marker\" body and single `blocked` `dead` event, and the lowest-owner rule.\n\n**Verifies:** task verify passes (9/9); `pnpm verify` passes end to end (3907 + 169 tests, typecheck, build, lint)."}}
